    a: "<b>HRCT pattern — usual interstitial pneumonia (UIP) / idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF):</b><br><b>Classic HRCT features of UIP (IPF):</b><ul><li><b>Honeycombing:</b> Clustered cystic air spaces (3–10 mm), peripheral subpleural, lower lobe predominance</li><li><b>Traction bronchiectasis:</b> Dilated airways in areas of fibrosis</li><li>Reticulation (fibrotic lines)</li><li>Subpleural, bibasilar distribution</li><li>Absence of: upper lobe predominance, extensive GGO without honeycombing, micronodules, bilateral air space consolidation</li></ul><b>ATS/ERS classification of HRCT in ILD:</b><ul><li>Typical UIP pattern → IPF without biopsy needed (if clinical context supports)</li><li>Indeterminate UIP → surgical lung biopsy to confirm</li></ul><b>Histopathological (biopsy) findings in UIP:</b><ul><li><b>Temporal heterogeneity:</b> Areas of old fibrosis (honeycombing) adjacent to areas of acute injury (fibroblastic foci)</li><li><b>Spatial heterogeneity:</b> Normal lung adjacent to fibrotic lung</li><li>Fibroblastic foci: active foci of myofibroblasts proliferating in areas of ongoing injury</li><li>Minimal inflammation (unlike NSIP which has diffuse inflammation)</li></ul><b>IPF treatment:</b> Nintedanib or pirfenidone (anti-fibrotic); avoid steroids (worsen outcomes)"
