    a: "<b>Hemolytic anemia workup:</b><br><b>Common to all hemolysis:</b><ul><li>Elevated <b>reticulocyte count</b> (bone marrow compensation)</li><li>Elevated <b>indirect (unconjugated) bilirubin</b> (RBC breakdown → heme → biliverdin → bilirubin)</li><li>Elevated <b>LDH</b> (released from RBCs)</li><li>Low/absent <b>haptoglobin</b> (binds free hemoglobin → complexes removed by liver)</li></ul><b>Intravascular hemolysis (RBCs lysed in bloodstream):</b><ul><li>Causes: G6PD deficiency (oxidative stress), PNH, cold agglutinin disease, TTP/HUS, mechanical hemolysis (prosthetic valves)</li><li>Additional findings: <b>hemoglobinemia</b> (pink plasma), <b>hemoglobinuria</b> (red/brown urine, dipstick +blood but no RBCs on microscopy), hemosiderinuria</li></ul><b>Extravascular hemolysis (RBCs removed by spleen/liver macrophages):</b><ul><li>Causes: AIHA (warm — IgG, Coombs+), hereditary spherocytosis, sickle cell disease</li><li>No hemoglobinuria (hemoglobin not released into plasma)</li></ul><b>Direct Coombs (DAT) test:</b><ul><li>Positive: antibody or complement on RBC surface → AIHA, drug-induced hemolysis, transfusion reaction</li><li>Negative: intrinsic RBC defect (spherocytosis, G6PD, PNH), microangiopathic (TTP)</li></ul>"
